   "narrative": "Scipio brings his army out of its camp onto the open plain. The legionary heavy infantry stands in the centre in three ranks: hastati in front, principes behind them and triarii last. Unlike the usual chessboard pattern, each maniple of principes sits directly behind a maniple of hastati, which leaves straight lanes through the line. The velites skirmish in those lanes. Masinissa's Numidian horse takes the right, Laelius's Roman and allied horse the left.",
