   "id": "elephants",
   "title": "The elephants are met",
   "time": "Midday",
   "narrative": "The velites run forward into the gap, throw javelins at the animals and fall back into the lanes. The Roman horns blare, and perhaps weapons beat on shields. Many elephants shy at the noise. Most of them plunge into the empty lanes, where javelins strike their flanks and those that emerge behind the army are hunted down. A few slam into the hastati and do real harm before they are driven off.",
